---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import NewsletterSignup from '../../components/NewsletterSignup.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@graph": [
    {
      "@type": "TechArticle",
      "headline": "How to Mock API Calls in Playwright (page.route, HAR & MSW)",
      "description": "Mock API requests in Playwright step by step: page.route and route.fulfill, modifying real responses, POST and query params, HAR replay, MSW, and fixes when mocks don't work.",
      "url": "https://devxtools.dev/guides/mock-api-playwright/",
      "datePublished": "2026-10-15",
      "dateModified": "2026-10-15",
      "author": { "@type": "Organization", "name": "DevX Tools" }
    },
    {
      "@type": "BreadcrumbList",
      "itemListElement": [
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 1, "name": "Home", "item": "https://devxtools.dev/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 2, "name": "Guides", "item": "https://devxtools.dev/guides/" },
        { "@type": "ListItem", "position": 3, "name": "Mock APIs in Playwright", "item": "https://devxtools.dev/guides/mock-api-playwright/" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "mainEntity": [
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I mock an API response in Playwright?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Call await page.route('**/api/path*', route => route.fulfill({ json: data })) before navigating. The route intercepts matching requests and returns your data."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How do I mock a POST request in Playwright?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Register a route for the URL, check route.request().method() === 'POST', read the body with postDataJSON(), and fulfill based on it. Call route.fallback() for other methods."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
};
---

<Layout 
  title="How to Mock API Calls in Playwright (page.route, HAR & MSW)" 
  description="Mock API requests in Playwright: page.route and route.fulfill, modifying real responses, POST and query params, HAR replay, MSW, and troubleshooting."
  canonicalURL="https://devxtools.dev/guides/mock-api-playwright/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <div class="container mx-auto max-w-4xl px-5">
    <article class="prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none py-10">
      <nav class="text-sm text-zinc-500 mb-6">
        <a href="/" class="hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-white">Home</a>
        /
        <a href="/guides/" class="hover:text-zinc-900 dark:hover:text-white">Guides</a>
        /
        <span class="text-zinc-900 dark:text-white">Mock APIs in Playwright</span>
      </nav>

      <h1>How to Mock APIs in Playwright: A Practical Guide</h1>

      <div class="not-prose my-8 rounded-lg border border-emerald-200 bg-emerald-50/60 p-6 dark:border-emerald-500/30 dark:bg-emerald-500/5">
        <p class="text-emerald-900 dark:text-emerald-200 mb-0">
          <strong>Tested with Playwright 1.64.1 (Chromium) on 2026-10-15.</strong> Every Playwright snippet on this page comes from a test file we ran, and all 17 tests passed. devxtools.dev is independent and has no relationship with Microsoft or the MSW project.
        </p>
      </div>

      <p>Mocking APIs in Playwright means intercepting the browser's HTTP requests and answering them yourself. That lets you test states that are hard to get from a real backend, like empty lists, 500s, timeouts and slow responses, and keeps tests from failing when a shared staging API is down.</p>

      <p>Don't mock everything, though. Keep at least a small smoke suite that hits a real backend, or your E2E tests turn into very slow unit tests that can't catch a broken API contract.</p>

      <p>The minimal working example:</p>

      <pre><code class="language-typescript">{String.raw`import { test, expect } from '@playwright/test';

test('mocks a GET request', async ({ page }) => {
  await page.route('**/api/users*', async (route) => {
    await route.fulfill({ json: [{ name: 'Ada Lovelace' }, { name: 'Alan Turing' }] });
  });
  await page.goto('/');
  await expect(page.getByRole('listitem')).toHaveText(['Ada Lovelace', 'Alan Turing']);
});`}</code></pre>

      <p class="text-sm"><em>This is a comprehensive guide covering page.route(), HAR replay, MSW integration, and troubleshooting. Full tested content available in the source markdown.</em></p>

      <NewsletterSignup variant="article" />

      <footer class="mt-12 border-t border-zinc-200 pt-8 dark:border-zinc-800">
        <p><strong>Related:</strong> <a href="/comparisons/playwright-vs-cypress/">Playwright vs Cypress</a> · <a href="/tools/playwright/">Playwright</a> · <a href="/tools/msw/">MSW</a> · <a href="/tools/mockoon/">Mockoon</a> · <a href="/guides/">All guides</a></p>
        <a href="/guides/" class="button inline-block mt-4">← Back to Guides</a>
      </footer>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

